Z||000000||qwert||04-11-2001||02:18 AM||||am interested in the conversion but would like your imput...what hp/torque combo you have...kill stories...are you satisfied or got gripes...I want to go into it with eyes open...thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||elfiero||04-11-2001||08:28 AM||||Here is my opinion;<BR>Start with archie's kit,get a crate350,budget<BR>2 times the money and time everyone tells<BR>you,then have some fun doing it yourself!.<BR>when you are done you will be sooo glad you<BR>made the swap!This is not rocket science,but<BR>is not like doing a tuneup either.be prepared<BR>to do some cutting on your baby as it is hard<BR>to put 10lbs of sh*t in a 5lb bag.It WILL fit<BR>but it sure don't look like it when the <BR>motor is sitting on the cradle.||||reg||6
Z||000002||Jay||04-11-2001||12:33 PM||||When my 86 GT's engine went I was considering a rebuild or a conversion to a 3.8 Supercharged.  While looking for the 3.8 I came across a 97 Northstar with tranny.  I'd seen John Normans conversion and a few in Michigan.  What the hell, I did it.  Best thing I ever did.  The engine is smooth as silk and tons of torque.  Even with the computer "problems" it was well worth it.<P>As was mentioned, do it yourself and save a boat load of money!  My conversion including the engine and tranny was under $10 000 Canadian, including suspension, rims, rubber, interior...in short, everything!!The work I couldn't do (like welding) I sourced out.  It's alot of fun and you really get to know your car.  This was the first engine conversion I've ever done on any car.  If I can do it, anyone can.<P>Jay<BR>1986 GT Norhtstar <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||qwert||04-12-2001||02:07 AM||||thanks for the suggestions guys...it is more what is the V8 capable of and its limitation in the Fiero platform...how does it run against domestic or high performance imports on the street.||||reg||1
Z||000004||elfiero||04-12-2001||09:47 AM||||Trust me,either the N* or a SBC WILL spank<BR>just about anything you can find on the street I've beaten vipers and vette's of all <BR>types.As far as handling,with a rear bar and<BR>aluminum cradle bushings,it feels like a very<BR>expensive italian pocket rocket.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Butter||04-12-2001||03:51 PM||||Go For It!<BR>I love the extra power.  I recomend over 300HP to get the full effect.  I drive my 2m8 almost everyday.||||reg||14
Z||000006||rprevo||04-12-2001||06:00 PM|||| I agree you gotta go 300 hp and up<BR>If you buy the GM Crate by the complete<BR>engine Intake mounts different.<BR>I didn't know this and got burned, Not to many vendors make this new mounting pattern.<BR>and I ended up back at the dealer buying<BR>an intake. Was 300 bucks!<P>Awsome car when you put in a little power for<BR>passing,<P><BR>   Ray||||reg||1
